# DC Motor Speed Control with Push Buttons

A simple project for controlling DC motor speed using two push buttons and an Arduino Uno. Based on this tutorial: https://youtu.be/fxgcnJJlTd4

## Description

This project controls the speed of a DC motor using an Arduino Uno and an L293D motor driver. Two push buttons are used to increase or decrease the motor speed (PWM value) in steps of 10.

- Button 1 → Increase speed by 10
- Button 2 → Decrease speed by 10

## Components

- Arduino Uno (1)
- L293D Motor Driver
- DC Motor (1)
- Push Buttons (2)
- Resistors (for pull-up/pull-down, if used)
- Breadboard and jumper wires
- External power supply for the motor

## Wiring

(fill in your actual pin connections, e.g.:)
