> ⚠️ Never power the motor directly from the Arduino — always use the motor driver with a separate power source for the motor.

## Code

The code is in `motor_control.ino`.

## How It Works

The current speed value is stored as a variable (e.g. `speed`), starting at some default value. Pressing Button 1 increases `speed` by 10, pressing Button 2 decreases it by 10 (with limits at 0 and 255). The value is then written to the L293D enable pin using `analogWrite()` to control motor speed via PWM.

